{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558963547,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf55b3bffeEvCBKbn8MNJrl7","part":{"id":"prt_1d40ca13b002JOBNKWVrwtQQbC","sessionID":"ses_e2bf55b3bffeEvCBKbn8MNJrl7","messageID":"msg_1d40c8d8600170HhNfzU0yOxN4","type":"text","text":"T010 complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n1. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\n   Added `describe('command attach on a deep-loop prompt')` with the four cases from the task line: the `/deep:ai-council` and `/deep:reviw` prompts expect `undefined`, while `run /deep:review now` and `review the parser in depth` expect `/deep:review`.\n\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`\n   The deep-loop gate now opens only when `typedCommandIn(prompt) === commands[workflowMode]` or `DEPTH_REQUEST` matches. The comment was rewritten to say typing another deep-loop command asks for that command, not this one.\n\n## Verify output\n\nBefore the gate change (test-first run):\n\n```\n × withholds the review command when another deep-loop command is named\n × withholds the review command when an unknown deep-loop command is named\n Tests  2 failed | 5 passed (7)\n```\n\nAfter the change:\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\nProbe lines 2–3 of `node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings $PL/probe-attach.mts | sed -n 2,3p`:\n\n```\nattachCommand(system-deep-loop, single review, 'what did /deep:ai-council decide') -> undefined\nattachCommand(system-deep-loop, single review, 'run /deep:review now') -> \"/deep:review\"\n```\n\nExtra guard (not named by the task): `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exited 0 with no diagnostics.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Nothing was left undone. The tasks.md checkbox was not ticked, per the brief.\n- No git state was touched. `git status` for the two named files shows `command-attach.ts` modified and the guard test untracked, both as expected (the test file and the `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` addition came from T009).","time":{"start":1794558959931,"end":1794558963547}}}
